index 00000000..75d2e2c6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/port/TRANSIENT_AUDIO.md
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+# Temporary-scene audio (experimental SDK1.13)
+
+A temporary-scene owner can play copied PCM through the same locked sound engine
+and SDL output as the native game. No additional device, OS player, game overlay
+function or guest-memory write is used. The eight new SDK pointers follow
+`transient_gl_proc`; the SDK1.12 table prefix and transient source layout remain
+unchanged. This is an experimental extension of the isolated transit runtime.
+
+`transient_audio_create` copies interleaved signed16 PCM, mono or stereo at
+8000–96000Hz. All structure `size` fields must be set. `frames` counts channel
+frames. Each lease holds at most16 clips,64 voices and256MiB of copied PCM, with
+at most600seconds per clip. Copying runs outside the audio lock; adoption is a
+bounded operation under that lock. Play, set, stop and render allocate nothing.
+
+The optional loop interval is `[loop_begin_frame, loop_end_frame)`, with end0
+meaning the full clip length. A loop plays its intro from frame0 once, then
+repeats the authored interval. A non-looping voice plays the full PCM clip.
+Native-rate conversion and pitch use linear interpolation at the existing
+48000Hz stereo output. Looping interpolation wraps to the loop's first frame.
+
+The active exclusive scene owner alone can create/release clips, play/update
+voices, stop a voice (handle0 means all its voices), pause the bus or query it.
+Unknown owners, stale handles, malformed descriptors and exceeded budgets fail
+without stealing resources. Clip/voice handles0 mean failure. Control/stat calls
+return `OPENRAC_HOOK_OK` or `OPENRAC_HOOK_UNKNOWN`; `playing` returns1/0.
+
+Voice parameters contain LOOP/PAUSED flags, group EFFECTS0 or MUSIC1, gain0–4,
+pitch.25–4 and pan−1–1. Centered stereo preserves both original channels. Group
+gain follows the native master-volume square law `(master/1024)^2`. The existing
+global output volume/mute is applied afterward by the normal output callback;
+the existing device lifecycle and recovery stay in use.
+
+The first successful PCM play takes over the host audio bus for the rest of the
+lease. Native SoundPlayer and native stream cursors then remain frozen. The bus
+does not return to the origin's music between effects or when its voices become
+silent. Bus pause emits silence and freezes all scene voice positions. Native
+host audio resumes at exactly its old cursors after scene end. Legacy1.12 scenes
+that never play PCM retain their previous audio behavior.
+
+The frontend runs deterministic audio ticks in `OPENRAC_AUDIO_TICKED` mode and
+watches the existing device in normal mode. A scene must close its resources in
+its closing callback. The host additionally clears every clip/voice on normal
+return, callback error, owner unload and window close, including the native
+quit path that exits without unwinding the synchronous call stack.
+
+`transient_audio_stats` reports clips, voices, bus pause, rendered/nonzero output
+frames and normalized peak for the actual PCM bus. These counters are **before
+global output gain**. They prove PCM mixing, not device audibility; device/mute
+proof requires a separate real-output test.
+
+Focused tests cover actual samples, authored intro/loop boundaries, sample-rate
+conversion, pitch, pan, native group gains, pause cursor preservation, owner and
+capacity guards, copied memory, zero render/play allocations, native VAG cursor
+freeze/resume and a real SDK1.13 DLL through the loader. The latter checks normal,
+nested, foreign-owner, error and consecutive-lease cleanup. Existing old-mod
+loader tests retain SDK1.5/1.10 compatibility coverage. These CPU checks do not
+replace native PAL/NTSC listening and output-capture tests.
